<Legal title="Terms and Conditions">
  <h2>1. What džingel is</h2>
  <p>
    džingel is a private place where a group of friends keeps its inside jokes together with the
    context that makes them funny. Only members of a group can see that group's quotes.
  </p>

  <h2>2. Your account</h2>
  <p>
    Choose a username and a password and keep the password to yourself. You are responsible for what
    happens under your account. Do not share it with others.
  </p>

  <h2>3. What you may add</h2>
  <p>
    Only add quotes that your friends would be happy to see. Do not add anything hateful, cruel,
    unlawful, or that shares private details such as addresses, phone numbers or photos. Remember
    that quotes are about real people, some of whom may be young.
  </p>

  <h2>4. Respect others</h2>
  <p>
    If someone asks you to remove a quote about them, please do so. Do not use džingel to bully or
    harass anyone.
  </p>

  <h2>5. Removal and changes</h2>
  <p>
    The operator may remove content or accounts that break these terms. These terms may change; the
    date at the top shows the current version.
  </p>

  <h2>6. No guarantees</h2>
  <p>
    džingel is provided as it is, without promises that it will always be available or free of
    errors. Keep your own copy of anything you cannot lose.
  </p>

  <h2>7. Contact</h2>
  <p>Questions about these terms go to the contact shown at the top of this page.</p>
  <p>See also the <a href="/privacy">Privacy notice</a>.</p>
</Legal>
